  "limitations": [
    "The global conditions for embedding a bendable piecewise smooth surface remain open in the general case (p. 141).",
    "The constructed bendable sphere has self-intersections in R\u00b3 and is neither embedded nor even immersed in R\u00b3 (p. 151).",
    "It is impossible to turn the constructed bendable torus inside out practically (p. 152)."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This theoretical paper substantiates the possibility of one-parameter bending for developable surfaces possessing a stationary curvilinear edge and stationary rectilinear generators. It details the mathematical conditions for developability and demonstrates how to construct such surfaces, including those with prescribed geodesic curvature. The study presents specific examples of bendable developable surfaces, such as a cone and truncated cone, and extends the concept to closed piecewise developable surfaces homeomorphic to a torus and a sphere. A key finding is that the intrinsic metric of a developable surface remains invariant during one-parameter bending, even as its external shape in R\u00b3 changes. The paper also identifies conditions that lead to rigid developments, such as when certain parameters reach infinity, and discusses practical limitations like the impossibility of physically turning a bendable torus inside out.",
